# Help: KVM host support on x86_64, for nested virtualization
#
# x86_64 KVM hypervisor with Intel VMX and AMD SVM support.
# Enables running VMs inside a QEMU guest (nested virtualization).
#
# MITIGATION_VMSCAPE keeps a guest from attacking the host's userspace
# VMM; it depends on KVM and sits under the CPU_MITIGATIONS menu.
#
# KVM_WERROR builds KVM with -Werror, the build every patch to KVM x86 must
# pass with KVM_INTEL=m and KVM_AMD=m; it depends on EXPERT, which
# core/core.config sets, and not on KASAN.
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/virt/kvm/index.html
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/hw-vuln/vmscape.html
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/process/maintainer-kvm-x86.html
CONFIG_VIRTUALIZATION=y
CONFIG_KVM=m
CONFIG_KVM_INTEL=m
CONFIG_KVM_AMD=m
CONFIG_KVM_WERROR=y
CONFIG_KVM_IOAPIC=y
CONFIG_KVM_SMM=y
CONFIG_CPU_MITIGATIONS=y
CONFIG_MITIGATION_VMSCAPE=y
